        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-29T00:21:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, this is how it works - compaction scans the entire storage and copies discovered valid objects in order it find them.",
      "parentUuid": "06f2be9b_5996abce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "961d2908006ae1ddeb4728590806a583c8640a8c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e3021e2_b9e202db",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-28T05:57:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "or we could add \u0027empty reserved objects that we haven\u0027t seen yet\u0027 (which will be different from values present in cache) after reaching the end of flash list",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "961d2908006ae1ddeb4728590806a583c8640a8c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "491365b7_a9b15d51",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-29T00:21:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the set of reserved objects is fixed, the provision above is just a failsafe mechanism to guarantee that we do not end up without a reserved object in flash as a result of some bug. Having the object in flash will guarantee that when commit time comes the actual value in the cache will be examined and compared with the one stored in the flash.\n\nSo, when we need to recover from cases when not reserved objects are found int the flash (mostly when recovering from catastrophic failures), we put into flash missing reserved objects with value of zero.",
      "parentUuid": "6e3021e2_b9e202db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "961d2908006ae1ddeb4728590806a583c8640a8c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
