        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-29T00:21:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In reality I am pretty sure we would never encounter a case where pre-migration TPM storage exceeds 10K: yes, there is room for 12K there, but this implementation stores some reserved objects in marshaled form, and this is guaranteed to save at least one kilobyte.\n\nIf existing data requires more than 10K the migration would fail without destroying the \u0027legacy\u0027 nvmem contents.",
      "parentUuid": "41866f7d_b7f970ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 177,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 177,
        "endChar": 27
      },
