        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-29T21:48:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, not not completely. I can easily see us dropping SHA1, SHA384 and SHA512, which we don\u0027t use in Chrome OS, to save space in the flash in the future.\n\nCan we at least add some compile-time checks that breaks in case we change the set of algos or the number of PCRs (e.g. check the size of s_pcrs[]?) to remind us to update this file.\n\nLike at the beginning of this file:\n/*\n * This implementation assumes 4 banks (SHA-1, 256, 384, 512) of 24 PCRs.\n * Will break otherwise.\n */\nstatic_assert(IMPLEMENTATION_PCR \u003d\u003d 24);\nstatic_assert(sizeof(PCR) \u003d\u003d  SHA1_DIGEST_SIZE + SHA256_DIGEST_SIZE + ...);",
      "parentUuid": "a78189bc_9704871e",
      "range": {
