      },
      "lineNbr": 1944,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-28T05:57:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so, we never actually check .generation here, relying instead on page numbers and transaction delimiters. \nbut when we do update_xxx it helps to make sure that we never attempt to delete the newly added one (generation+1), in case something is wrong and we never find the old copy (generation). is that the rationale for still keeping .generation in the header?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1944,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1944,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "961d2908006ae1ddeb4728590806a583c8640a8c",
