      "lineNbr": 1989,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T20:14:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "verify_last_section() at the end does\n  if (ch-\u003econtainer_type !\u003d NN_OBJ_TRANSACTION_DEL) return EC_ERROR_INVAL;\nwhich will cause verify_delimiter() to return an error, the loop in retrieve_nvmem_contents() will break, and we\u0027ll get to the code that currently doesn\u0027t wipe out anything, but can be easily modified to do that in the future.\n  /*\n   * Something is really messed up, need to wipe out and start\n   * from scratch?\n   */\n  ccprintf(\"%s:%d FAILURE!\\n\", __func__, __LINE__);\n\nThis is a fringe case when container_type !\u003d NN_OBJ_TRANSACTION_DEL \u0026\u0026 container_type !\u003d NN_OBJ_OLD_COPY, while container_type_copy \u003d\u003d NN_OBJ_TRANSACTION_DEL. Iiuc, it can\u0027t happen due to a sudden power loss (thanks to checking type_copy). So, maybe potentially wiping everything is ok.",
      "parentUuid": "da598741_9a55bacf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1989,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 1989,
        "endChar": 28
      },
